From my own knowledge: The user wants an Arduino sketch that blinks an LED on pin 13 every 500 milliseconds (half a second) using `millis()` timing, avoiding the `delay()` function. This is a standard pattern for creating a non-blocking loop.

Here is the code:

<title>
// Blink LED on Pin 13 every 500ms using millis()
const int ledPin = 13;
const unsigned long interval = 500;   // milliseconds

unsigned long lastChange = 0;         // Track time in millis()

void setup() {
  pinMode(ledPin, OUTPUT);
}

void loop() {
  unsigned long now = millis();

  // Check if enough time has passed since the last blink
  if (now - lastChange >= interval) {
    lastChange = now;
    digitalWrite(ledPin, HIGH);
    // Turn off after the blink
    digitalWrite(ledPin, LOW);
  }

  // Other code can go here
}
